==Battleground==
*3 [[Hyppoh]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Lione Hippoe]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Lione Hippoe]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*1 [[Lione Hippoe]] spawns after 56 seconds<sup>1,680f</sup>.
*1 [[Lione Hippoe]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Shibalien]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Shibalien]]s (1,000%) spawn, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
**4 [[Lione Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
**8 [[Lione Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
**2 [[Lucky Sloth]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**2 [[Lucky Sloth]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**3 [[Cyberhorn]]s spawn, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
With the sheer number of buffed Alien enemies in this level, it's not recommended to attempt it until all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from [[Into the Future]] have been obtained.

At least three [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]] are recommended to hold the line against the flurry of Hippoe variants, with [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]] and [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] being recommended for the Lione Hippoe and Hyppoh, respectively. Any decent ranged [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Anti-Aliens]] the player has should be brought to deal with Cyberhorn, with some good examples being [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]. Lucky Sloth can be dealt with via decent [[:Category:Backliner-class Cats|backliners]] like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] and variants thereof, as well as [[:Category:Waver-class Cats|wavers]] like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]], who can also aid in getting rid of the peons.

Later-game players can utilize [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Anti-Traitless Cats]] to get the stage over with quicker, with [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]] and [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] being good options. Do bear in mind that Hitman needs a stepping stone to hit Lucky Sloth without getting damaged in return, however.

